ndia, enacted on January 26, 1950, represents a monumental document in the landscape of global governance, establishing the framework for the world's largest democracy. Drafted by the Constituent Assembly led by figures such as B.R. Ambedkar and Jawaharlal Nehru, it emerged from the struggle against colonial rule and reflects the aspirations of a diverse nation, encompassing over a billion people across various cultures and languages. Its significance lies not only in its legal stipulations but also in its role as a symbol of unity in a nation characterized by its vast social and ethnic plurality.

